**Implementation (complete, verified):**
Added `pub fn rename` to `src/store.rs:40-91`. It compiles cleanly and passes `cargo clippy`. The function:
- Errors (`NotFound`) if no `{old_id}.note` exists.
- Reads and parses the file the same way `load_all` does (`splitn(4, SEP)`), and errors (`InvalidInput`) if the stored first field doesn't match `old_id` (guards against a file whose content id disagrees with its filename).
- Errors (`AlreadyExists`) if a file for `new_id` already exists and isn't the same file.
- Rebuilds the content with `new_id`/`new_title`, preserving the `pinned_flag` and `body` (tags are derived from body on load, so they're preserved automatically).
- Writes `{new_id}.note`, then removes `{old_id}.note` — but only when `new_id != old_id`, so a same-id rename just updates the title in place.

After `rename`, `load_all(dir)` returns exactly one note with the new id/title, and there's no trace of the old id on disk.

